/*  EXPECTED: COMPILES and runs; compiled output must match the interpreter.

    An outer series grows inside a rabbit, and what is inserted is also from outside.

    Nothing here outlives its region: the series was made outside the rabbit and is only
    GROWN inside it. The compiled program used to give it a new buffer in the rabbit, which
    the rabbit's Done. then freed. A series grows in the region it was made in now
    (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O3). */

Define first as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
Define keeper as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Insert first into keeper.
Done.

/*  Make and drop enough values that freed memory is handed out again. */
Define churn as a series of text.
Define tick as 0.
While tick is less than 400, repeat:
    Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
    tick becomes tick + 1.
Done.
State keeper.
